1996-12)",[60,65,70,75,79,82,86,90],{"met_days":61,"type":62,"label":63,"description":64},0,"launch","Launch — Delta II 7925","Cape Canaveral, 1996-12-04. Mars Pathfinder carried the first rover to operate on Mars — Sojourner, a 10.5-kg microwave-oven-sized vehicle. The mission also demonstrated airbag-cushioned EDL — a radical lower-cost alternative to the heritage Viking propulsive landing.",{"met_days":66,"type":67,"label":68,"description":69},0.005,"tli_or_tmi","Trans-Mars injection","Delta II second stage burn sends Pathfinder on a 7-month Mars transfer.",{"met_days":71,"type":72,"label":73,"description":74},30,"tcm","TCM-1","First post-TMI cleanup burn.",{"met_days":76,"type":72,"label":77,"description":78},48.76,"TCM-2","Mid-cruise refinement.",{"met_days":80,"type":72,"label":81,"description":78},86.92,"TCM-3",{"met_days":83,"type":72,"label":84,"description":85},100,"TCM-4 — final pre-EDL","Final approach targeting for the Ares Vallis EDL site.",{"met_days":12,"type":87,"label":88,"description":89},"arrival","Mars approach + cruise-stage separation","1997-07-04 — Independence Day. Cruise stage separated; the backshell entered Mars's atmosphere at 7.3 km/s.",{"met_days":91,"type":92,"label":93,"description":94},212.005,"edl_or_oi","Mars EDL — airbag landing in Ares Vallis","First-ever airbag landing on Mars. After parachute + retrorockets, the airbag-cocooned lander bounced 15+ times across the Ares Vallis floodplain before rolling to a stop. Sojourner deployed via the lander's solar-panel ramps and roamed for 83 sols, returning the first wheeled mobility data from another planet. Communications lost 1997-09-27 probably due to battery failure.",{"source_tier":96,"reference_frame":97,"departure_body":98,"arrival_body":99,"transfer_type":100,"tcm_count":46,"waypoints_helio_au":101},"tier_1_5_hybrid","heliocentric_ecliptic_J2000","earth","mars","type1_lambert",[102,105,109,113,117,121,125,129,133,137,141,145,149,153,156,160,164,168,172,176,180,184,188,191,195,1