61,436],188.8772,-0.968084,-1.107795,[438,439,61,440],191.1257,-0.949718,-1.13094,[442,443,61,444],193.3743,-0.930941,-1.153596,[446,447,61,448],195.6228,-0.91174,-1.175727,[450,451,61,452],197.8713,-0.892099,-1.19729,[454,455,61,456],200.1199,-0.872084,-1.218352,[458,459,61,460],202.3684,-0.851669,-1.238855,[462,463,61,464],204.6169,-0.830871,-1.258799,[466,467,61,468],206.8655,-0.809735,-1.278233,[470,471,61,472],209.114,-0.788224,-1.297076,[91,474,61,475],-0.760092,-1.32053,[477,478,61,479],213.6111,-0.754106,-1.323958,[481,478,61,479],215.8596,[483,478,61,479],218.1082,[485,478,61,479],220.3567,[487,478,61,479],222.6053,"Mars Pathfinder","LANDER · ROVER · FLOWN","First wheels on Mars; demonstrated airbag landing","Mars Pathfinder was NASA’s proof that landing on Mars did not have to cost a fortune. Instead of the retrorocket hover the Vikings used, it hit the atmosphere behind a heat shield, popped a parachute, inflated a cocoon of airbags, and bounced about fifteen times across the surface before rolling to a stop and opening like a flower. Out drove Sojourner — a rover the size of a microwave, the first wheels ever to turn on another planet. The science was modest; the point was the method. The airbag landing and the faster-cheaper-better approach it proved became the template for the far more ambitious rovers — Spirit and Opportunity — that followed.","The mission that proved cheap interplanetary missions could work. Pathfinder used a novel airbag landing system — bouncing about fifteen times across the surface before coming to rest — and delivered Sojourner, the first rover to operate on another planet. Sojourner traversed 100 m, examined a dozen rocks, and worked far past its 8-sol design lifetime. Pathfinder operated for nearly three months (85 days); the mission's success revived NASA's interplanetary programme after the failures of the 1990s.",[494,498,500,503,507],{"met":61,"label":495,"note":496,"type":497},"LAUNCH","Delta II 7925 from Cape Canaveral.","nominal",{"met":71,"label":73,"note":499,"type":497},"First trajectory correction.",{"met":12,"label":501,"note":502,"type":497},"EDL","Direct atmospheric entry — no orbit insertion. Heat shield, parachute, retro-rockets, then airbag inflation.",{"met":504,"label":505,"note":506,"type":497},212.01,"TOUCHDOWN","Lander bounces 15 times across Ares Vallis before coming to rest.",{"met":508,"label":509,"note":510,"type":511},213,"SOJOURNER DEPLOYED","First wheels on another planet.","info","/orrery/images/missions/mars-pathfinder/04.webp"],"uses":{"params":["id"]}}]}
